    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## What the change does\n\nPer the spec, a new owner's `membershipLevel` is now capped at **one above the current maximum `membershipLevel` among their existing household members** (owners sharing the same deterministic `householdId`, derived from normalized lastName + postcode). With no existing household member, no cap applies.\n\n## Changes made\n\n1. **`OwnerMembership.level()`** \u2014 after banding points into a level, applies the owner's stored `membershipLevelCap` (`min(level, cap)`); a null cap leaves the level unchanged.\n\n2. **New `CapMembershipLevel` function** \u2014 computes the cap at create time: the max level among existing household members `+ 1`, or leaves it null when the household has no prior member. It runs after `AssignHouseholdId` (needs `householdId`) and before `SaveOwner` (so `findAll()` returns only predecessors), mirroring the existing `AssignHouseholdId`/`CountNamesakes` pattern.\n\n3. **`Owner` entity + all four `schema.sql` files** \u2014 added the persisted `membership_level_cap` column, so the capped level is reflected on later `GET`s (consistent with how `householdSize`/`namesakeCount` are stored).\n\n4. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the `capMembershipLevel` step into the pipeline under `transaction` governance.\n\n5. **`EnsureIdentityUnique`** \u2014 the feature requires households with multiple members, but this duplicate check was rejecting *any* second owner in an existing household. I aligned it with `OwnerIdentity`'s documented single-source-of-truth (\"two owners are duplicates only when their whole identityKey is equal; same-household owners with different telephones are both allowed\"), so it now blocks on an exact full `identityKey` match rather than household alone. This is what lets a household legitimately hold more than one member.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreCapsLevelByHousehold` test (and the full suite) passes; the audit log confirms two same-household owners now create successfully at levels 1 and 2.",
